### Variables
@host = http://localhost:8081

### Login — correct password (expect 200 + Set-Cookie: JSESSIONID, AuthResponse body)
POST {{host}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manager@example2.com",
  "password": "TestPass123!"
}

### Login — wrong password (expect 401 {"error":"Invalid email or password"})
POST {{host}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "manager@example.com",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### Me — unauthenticated, no cookie sent (expect 401 {"error":"Authentication required"})
GET {{host}}/api/me

### Me — authenticated (run the first "Login" request above in the same IntelliJ HTTP Client
### session first — it stores the session cookie automatically and this request reuses it)
GET {{host}}/api/me

### Logout (expect 200)
POST {{host}}/api/logout

###
GET {{host}}/api/raise-requests/mine